# A new run picks its world by clicking a moon, and gets that moon's world.
#
# Deliberately runs WITHOUT --seed. That flag pins the world on the command line and so skips this
# screen entirely — which is exactly what keeps the other hundred-odd scripts working — so a script
# testing the screen cannot pass it. The run is still reproducible: the sky is drawn from a constant
# (Config.SkyCloud.SkySeed), so moon 0 is Armoth in every process, and confirming it reseeds the run
# to Armoth's world seed. Everything after the confirmation is as deterministic as --seed made it.
#
# The three assertions, in order: the screen exists and is reached by New; CANCEL goes back without
# spending anything; and CONFIRM really does hand the run the world the moon names — read off the
# live run's own seed rather than off the screen that claimed it.
#
# FLAGS: --playground --skip-childhood --debug --no-encounters --location-type test --location-id 0 --npc-static --period noon

wait
click menu New
wait mode WorldSelection 20

# Nothing chosen yet: the box is up with both its readings empty, and `regions` reports CONFIRM
# dead — a disabled button differs only by colour, which `expect` cannot see.
expect THE MOONS
regions

# Backing out costs nothing and returns to the menu.
click world cancel
wait mode MainMenu 20

# In again, and this time pick one. `click moon` turns the sky towards it first, exactly as the
# arrow pad would, and then hovers and clicks it through the real screen-space picking.
click menu New
wait mode WorldSelection 20
click moon Armoth

# One settle before reading the screen: the box is repainted from Update, so a `regions` or an
# `expect` fired in the same breath as the click reads the frame before it.
wait
expect Armoth
expect -209322086

# Pointing at a SECOND moon must not disturb the first. The two states are drawn differently in the
# sky — chosen is larger and white, pointed-at smaller and yellow — and the box reads them on
# separate lines, which is the half of it a script can see.
point moon Belavel
wait
expect Chosen
expect Armoth
expect Belavel

# Pressing empty sky releases the choice without leaving the screen: CONFIRM goes dead again, and
# `regions` says so.
click sky
wait
regions

# Take it back and go on.
click moon Armoth
wait

# The compass turns the camera. Asserted through the CLI's own report of the yaw either side of the
# press, since the camera is not something `dump` can see.
click arrow left
click arrow up

# Take it. The world is generated here, not before.
click world confirm
wait mode ProtagonistCreation 20
click continue
wait mode WorldView 60

# The run is being played in Armoth's world — the seed the moon stands for, not a time-based one.
expect-state save seed=-209322086
world

quit
